            0.081
          ],
          "content": "The Other Side of Zero"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.388,
            0.121,
            0.56,
            0.139
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Teacher’s Note"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.142,
            0.814,
            0.278
          ],
          "content": "Talk about thermometers and how they are used to measure temperature. Bring a laboratory thermometer to the class and measure the temperature of hot water and cold water. Point out to children that there are markings in the thermometer that are below $0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathbb { C } ,$ . Have a discussion on what $0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathbb { C }$ indicates, namely, the freezing point of water."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.317,
            0.56,
            0.343
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "10.4 Explorations with Integers"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.356,
            0.377,
            0.379
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "A hollow integer grid"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.288,
            0.382,
            0.488,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": "| 4 | -1 | -3 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| -3 |  | 1 |\n| -1 | -1 | 2 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
